**/.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
# A deployer's own local env file. `adapters/hermes/.env.template` IS committed and shipped; the
# `.env` beside it is that template filled in with their tokens and must never be committed. The
# monorepo root ignores `.env` globally, but THIS file is the one that ships (the generator copies it
# as the public repo's .gitignore), so without this line a user who follows LOCAL-SETUP.md sees their
# own credentials file sitting untracked in `git status`. Belt to the publish-time IGNORED guard.
adapters/hermes/.env
sotto-bridge/core/target/
.DS_Store
# Bridge build/release artifacts (build-app.sh + release.sh outputs — never committed;
# users get the app via the signed DMG on GitHub Releases)
sotto-bridge/app/Sotto Bridge.app/
sotto-bridge/app/Sotto-Bridge-*.dmg
sotto-bridge/app/.build/
# Bridge access-code signing key — the ED25519 private key that mints access codes. Its durable home
# is the GitHub Actions secret SOTTO_BRIDGE_SIGNING_KEY; the working copy lives at
# ~/.sotto/bridge-signing.key (0600), OUTSIDE any checkout. These patterns are the belt to that
# braces, and tools/prepare-public-repo.sh's SECRETS guard is the third layer.
**/bridge-signing.key
**/*signing.key
**/bridge-access-codes.log
# ship.sh markers: monorepo commit of the last Bridge DMG released from this machine + the
# remembered notarytool keychain-profile name. (There is no remembered template URL: the Deploy
# button is the committed DEFAULT_TEMPLATE_URL in tools/publish-public.sh, so both release lanes
# publish the same one.)
sotto-bridge/.last-ship
sotto-bridge/.notary-profile
# The Golden Corpus — the owner's real history, pseudonymized. "Scrubbed" never means "shareable":
# it lives on his infrastructure only (docs/plans/golden-corpus.md), is deleted by
# tools/prepare-public-repo.sh, and is guarded there (CORPUS GUARD). The identity map lives on the
# volume ($SOTTO_DATA/corpus-keys/), outside any checkout, and is never needed to run evals.
sotto-chief-of-staff/evals/corpus/
*.map.json
